title: "AI-Assisted Social Science Research: A Reason-Provenance Resource and Worked Case Study"
authors:
  - family-names: "Rudkin"
    given-names: "Simon"
    affiliation: "Department of Social Statistics, University of Manchester"
version: "0.3.1"
abstract: >-
  A social-science-facing resource on generative-AI-assisted research. The
  resource connects reason provenance, empirical verification, adversarial
  challenge, claim authorisation and manuscript governance using a documented
  PISA project and the Academic Writing Filter.
keywords:
  - "social science"
  - "generative AI"
  - "research methods"
  - "reason provenance"
  - "manuscript governance"
  - "claim preservation"
  - "research transparency"
  - "AI-assisted research"
  - "PISA"
